## sn5.8
sn5.8:1.1 | S: At Sāvatthī. | T: At Savatthi.
sn5.8:1.2 | S: Then the nun Sīsupacālā robed up in the morning … | T: Then, in the morning, the bhikkhuni Sisupacala dressed …
sn5.8:1.3 | S: and sat at the root of a tree for the day’s meditation. | T: she sat down at the foot of a tree for the day’s abiding.
sn5.8:1.4 | S: Then Māra the Wicked went up to Sīsupacālā and said to her, | T: Then Mara the Evil One approached the bhikkhuni Sisupacala and said to her:
